MINIBAK - SHORT INSTALLATION GUIDE
==================================
(Full documentation: README.md)

REQUIREMENTS
  - Debian or Ubuntu with systemd (tested on Debian 13)
  - Root access (the scripts ask for sudo themselves)
  - Internet or local mirror for rsync (installed automatically if missing)
  - The files install.sh, minibak.sh and conf in ONE directory

1. CONFIGURE
     nano conf
   Set at least:
     dir_src="/path/to/back/up"
     dir_dest="/path/for/the/backups"     (must not be inside dir_src)
     bool_timerEnabled=true               (true = scheduled backups, false = manual only)
   Optional: dir_log (default /var/log), int_keepFullWeeks (default 4)

2. INSTALL
     chmod +x install.sh
     ./install.sh
   Read the list of changes and answer "y". Everything is also written to
   install.log. Re-running the installer overwrites /etc/minibak.conf.

3. CHECK
     ls -l /usr/bin/minibak /etc/minibak.conf /etc/systemd/system/minibak.*
     systemctl list-timers minibak.timer      (next run: 00:00 / 12:00)

4. FIRST BACKUP
     minibak -c default
     ls <dir_dest>                            (a directory backup_YYYY-MM-DD_hh-mm-ss)

5. DAY-TO-DAY
     minibak -c default                       run a backup now
     minibak -c default -x                    apply changes of the timer/bool_timerEnabled
                                              made in /etc/minibak.conf (no backup is made)
     less /var/log/minibak.log                log
     journalctl -u minibak.service            output of scheduled runs
     minibak -h                               help

6. RESTORE
     rsync -aH <dir_dest>/backup_<timestamp>/<name of dir_src>/ /restore/target/

7. UNINSTALL
     ./install.sh uninstall
   Four optional questions (all default to "no"): remove rsync, delete logs,
   delete configuration, clear /tmp/minibak. The backups themselves are never deleted.
